---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import { offers } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Competitive Response Sprint"
  description="Turn verified competitive intelligence into battlecards, pricing responses, positioning, messaging and market action."
  path="/strategic-blueprint/"
>
  <section class="rsp13-hero" data-surface="dark">
    <div class="container rsp13-hero__inner">
      <span class="label">COMPETITIVE RESPONSE SPRINT</span>
      <h1>Turn the decision into a competitive response.</h1>
      <p>When the intelligence is clear but the response is not, Evidence Axis converts the findings into the sales, pricing, positioning and messaging assets needed to act.</p>
      <div class="rsp13-actions"><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=response">Discuss a Response Sprint <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/competitor-brief/">Start from the Decision Sprint →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container rsp13-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="label">WHEN THIS ENGAGEMENT FITS</span>
          <h2>You know what the market is doing. Now the team needs to respond.</h2>
          <p class="rsp13-lede">The Response Sprint starts from a defined competitive problem. It is for teams that need usable market-facing assets, not another research document.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rsp13-panel"><small class="mono">ENGAGEMENT</small><strong>{offers.responseSprint.priceDisplay}</strong><p>{offers.responseSprint.priceNote}.</p><small class="mono">DELIVERY</small><b>{offers.responseSprint.delivery}</b></aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section rsp13-muted">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">POSSIBLE SCOPE</span>
        <div class="rsp13-cards">
          <article><b>01</b><h3>Battlecards</h3><p>Competitor-specific sales guidance grounded in verified differences and bounded claims.</p></article>
          <article><b>02</b><h3>Objection handling</h3><p>Response language for the objections and comparisons most likely to appear in live deals.</p></article>
          <article><b>03</b><h3>Pricing response</h3><p>Options for packaging, pricing story and value justification where competitive pressure is visible.</p></article>
          <article><b>04</b><h3>Positioning response</h3><p>Sharper differentiation around the evidence-supported areas that matter to the target buyer.</p></article>
          <article><b>05</b><h3>Messaging architecture</h3><p>Claims, proof points and boundaries that can travel across sales and marketing without outrunning evidence.</p></article>
          <article><b>06</b><h3>Enablement</h3><p>Competitor-specific assets and an executive review of what changed, why it matters and how to use the response.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container rsp13-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="label">DEPENDENCY</span>
          <h2>The response inherits the evidence standard.</h2>
          <p class="rsp13-lede">A strong response can be decisive without pretending every claim is certain. Facts remain sourced, strategic interpretation remains labeled, and unsupported assertions do not become sales copy simply because they sound useful.</p>
          <a class="rsp13-link" href="/method/">See the Evidence Axis method →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="rsp13-rule"><b>PUBLIC EVIDENCE</b><span>+</span><b>CLIENT CONTEXT</b><span>→</span><strong>COMPETITIVE RESPONSE</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section rsp13-final" data-surface="dark">
      <div class="container"><span class="label">RESPOND</span><h2>Bring the decision. We’ll scope the response.</h2><p>Tell us what the team needs to change in market, sales, pricing, positioning or messaging.</p><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=response">Discuss a Response Sprint <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .rsp13-hero{padding:clamp(5rem,10vw,8rem) 0;background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.rsp13-hero__inner{max-width:70rem}.rsp13-hero h1{max-width:13ch;margin:.8rem 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,6.2rem);line-height:.94;letter-spacing:-.055em}.rsp13-hero p{max-width:53rem;color:#cbd8e8;font-size:1.18rem;line-height:1.7}.rsp13-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin-top:1.7rem}.rsp13-actions>a:not(.btn),.rsp13-link{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:750;text-decoration:none}.rsp13-actions>a:not(.btn){color:#dbe8ff}.rsp13-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(16rem,.75fr);gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem);align-items:start}.rsp13-grid h2,.rsp13-final h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4.5vw,4.2rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:.6rem 0 1rem}.rsp13-lede{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text-muted)}.rsp13-panel{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--surface-border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--bg-raised);display:grid;gap:.45rem}.rsp13-panel strong{font:800 2rem/1 var(--font-display)}.rsp13-panel small{color:var(--text-faint);letter-spacing:.08em;margin-top:.65rem}.rsp13-panel p{margin:0;color:var(--text-muted)}.rsp13-muted{background:var(--bg-raised)}.rsp13-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem;margin-top:1.4rem}.rsp13-cards article{padding:1.35rem;border:1px solid var(--surface-border);border-radius:.85rem;background:var(--bg)}.rsp13-cards b{font-family:var(--font-mono);color:var(--accent);font-size:.72rem}.rsp13-cards h3{margin:.6rem 0 .45rem}.rsp13-cards p{margin:0;color:var(--text-muted);line-height:1.6}.rsp13-rule{display:grid;gap:.75rem;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--surface-border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--bg-raised);font-family:var(--font-mono)}.rsp13-rule span{color:var(--text-faint)}.rsp13-rule strong{color:var(--accent)}.rsp13-final{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.rsp13-final p{color:#cbd8e8;max-width:42rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem}@media(max-width:820px){.rsp13-grid,.rsp13-cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
